      "value": "@{5ae4f9f6801fa451b10edafc|full_name}: while i agree its the os's job to do this. windows infact still loves to toss all things on core 0 and 1. This issue effects vrchat dis-proportionally due to its weak multi threading. The benefits of changing cores on vrchat on ryzen chips specifically can increase fps in the upwards of 2-9%. \nThis is just a failure on windows, but something vrchat could help address by allowing core assignments on launch options.",
